{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.binding_eq_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.binding_eq_defect","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L66-L66","doc":"**Conjectural mass-defect factorisation.**  The bulk binding\nenergy is `E₀` times the Markov-trace defect between the free and\nthe bound braid:\n`binding wFree wAtom = E₀ · (|tr_M(W_free)| − |tr_M(W_atom)|)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.binding","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The bulk binding energy of an atom, as a function of its\nfree-nucleon braid `wFree` and bound atomic braid `wAtom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.E0_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.E0_pos","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L58-L58","doc":"`E₀` is a positive energy scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.E0","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The single archimedean calibration constant `E₀` (fibre functor\n`τ : R → ℝ`), fixed by one reference experiment; positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.traceMag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.traceMag","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Magnitude of the Jones–Markov trace `|tr_M(W)|` of a closed braid,\nindexed abstractly by a braid identifier.  Real-valued because the\nabsolute value is the archimedean realisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/KnotFactorFrobeniusPairing.lean#L37-L68","doc":"**Conjecture class** (`conj:knot-factor-frobenius-pairing`).\n\nAn instance supplies a Markov-trace magnitude `traceMag` on closed\nbraids (the `|tr_M(·)|` of the categorical mass identity) and the\nsingle calibration constant `E₀`, and asserts that the bulk binding\nenergy `binding` of an atom is the calibrated Markov-trace defect\nbetween the free-nucleon braid `wFree` and the bound atomic braid\n`wAtom`.\n\nThe field `binding_eq_defect` carries the conjecture's genuine content\n(the mass-defect factorisation), not a bare `True`.  This is a\n**primary** conjecture (no other conjecture class in its signature). ","signatureChunk":0}]}